/* Glass's material: everything drawn is made of these names, and nothing
   else. Colours come in a light and a dark. Type is set as the rule's
   surface sets it by default: the prose in a sans, the headings in a serif
   that stands half again over it and rises by 1.4 a level, a line of 600px, spaced at 1.45 of
   the serif's size. Each face is sized to the serif's x-height, so the sans
   reads as large as the serif would. */

/* The faces, served with glass itself, so reading them tells no one else
   who reads: Source Serif 4, whose optical sizes draw a heading as a heading
   and a word in a line as a word, Source Sans 3 for the prose, and Source
   Code Pro. Latin only; what they lack falls to the faces beneath them. */

